# Labs and Experiments — {{TITLE}}

Labs turn claims about {{TOPIC}} into reproducible evidence. Start with observation and simulation, then make the smallest reversible change.

## Lab contract

Every substantial lab records:

- environment, versions, and authorization boundary;
- baseline and raw output;
- learner's prediction or hypothesis;
- one bounded change;
- verification and comparison;
- result, including failure;
- rollback or cleanup; and
- evidence links.

Never infer a successful command, build, test, experiment, or rollback. Use [[practice/_lab-template|the lab template]], append actuals to [[tracking/lab-log.csv|the lab log]], and advance through [[practice/LAB_LADDER|the lab ladder]] only when gate evidence exists.
